 "result": "All in `src/tessel/views.py`:\n\n1. **`VerbView.__init_subclass__`** (line 165) runs when you define a subclass. It scans for `get`, `post`, and the other names in `http_method_funcs`, and sets `cls.methods` to the matching uppercase verbs (e.g. `{\"GET\", \"POST\"}`). Methods inherited from base classes are included.\n\n2. **`View.to_view_func(name, *args, **kwargs)`** (line 86, classmethod) builds the plain view function:\n   - The inner `view(**kwargs)` instantiates the class (per request, or once if `init_every_request = False`) and calls `self.run_view(**kwargs)` through `active_app.ensure_sync`.\n   - It applies `decorators`, then attaches `view_class`, `methods`, and `provide_automatic_options` to the function. The route registration (`app.attach_route_rule`) uses `methods` to decide which verbs the URL accepts.\n\n3. **`VerbView.run_view`** (line 182) does the per-method routing. It looks up `getattr(self, request.method.lower())`, falls back to `get` for `HEAD` if there is no `head` handler, and calls the handler with the URL kwargs.\n\nThe base `View.run_view` (line 78) just raises `NotImplementedError`. `VerbView` overrides it to do the dispatch.",
